## Count the right thing

| Count | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| 130 official catalogue entries | 37 GOV.UK components, 38 NHS components, 13 NHS patterns and 42 publishing components, patterns and templates |
| 28 shared GOV.UK and NHS routes | Two source entries already point to one local page; these are not duplicate local implementations |
| 68 component pages | Existing component URLs reviewed individually |
| 58 main guides for those components | A maintenance owner for shared rules; distinct interaction variants remain documented |
| 263 examples | Inspectable documentation specimens, with every example linked to an owning guide and its other references |

The machine-readable [organisation record](../reference/component-rationalisation.json) also maps all 147 baseline guides and all 130 source entries. Its 108 owners across the whole guide set include patterns, foundations and governance pages. That number is not a count of installed components.

## Separate the layers

**Components** define a repeatable interaction or presentation: a button, field, breadcrumb, status tag or table. **Patterns** combine components for a task, such as checking answers or recovering from a failed request. **Page templates** organise authored information, such as a guide, collection or finder. A publishing template does not install a backend or replace a native automation editor.

Home Assistant has a further layer of native domain controls and task flows. A light colour picker, climate control, entity selector or schedule editor needs its own capability and state contract. The [missing-specification register](missing-components.html) links the 30 completed specifications without describing existing native features as missing.

## Implemented organisation

Each proposal has a stable identifier, evidence and acceptance criteria. Priorities describe the order of design work: **P1** protects task meaning, consequential actions or coverage claims; **P2** improves consistency and maintenance. The original proposals and acceptance criteria remain below as a review record; each item links to its implemented resolution.

<% audit['findings'].each do |finding| %>
<h3 id="<%= escape(finding['id'].downcase) %>"><%= escape(finding['id']) %>: <%= escape(finding['title']) %></h3>
<p><strong><%= escape(finding['priority']) %> · <%= escape(finding['status'].tr('-', ' ')) %>.</strong> <%= escape(finding['proposal']) %></p>
<% if finding['resolution'] %><p><strong>Resolution:</strong> <%= escape(finding['resolution']['summary']) %></p><% end %>
<p>Affected guides: <% finding['surfaces'].each_with_index do |url, index| %><%= ', ' unless index.zero? %><a href="<%= docs_path(url) %>"><%= escape(pages_by_url.fetch(url)['title']) %></a><% end %>.</p>
<ul><% finding['acceptanceCriteria'].each do |check| %><li><%= escape(check) %></li><% end %></ul>
<p>Rule dependencies: <% finding['ruleDependencies'].each_with_index do |rule, index| %><%= ', ' unless index.zero? %><a href="<%= docs_path(rule['localPath']) %>"><%= escape(rule['id']) %></a><% end %>.</p>
<% end %>

