## Preserve URLs and distinct behaviour

The 39 route relationships across the whole guide set keep their existing pages. The shared family navigation points directly to each owner and related variant. No route or fragment is removed; a future redirect still requires an explicit equivalence and migration review.

Keep the withdrawn NHS review-date page as a source record and distinguish its editorial review schedule from actual publication history. Keep the legacy lighting-card registration as a runtime compatibility alias: changing a guide's owner must not break saved dashboards.

An accordion remains different from a single details disclosure. A chapter link remains different from result-page pagination. A notification count remains different from a state tag or urgent alert. Their shared visual rules do not erase those meanings.

